## Strategic Initiatives

### Initiative 1: 100% Renewable Energy (2028)

**Current:** 65% | **Target:** 100%

| Site | Current | 2028 Target | Approach |
|------|---------|-------------|----------|
| US Operations | 72% | 100% | PPA, on-site solar |
| European Operations | 85% | 100% | Grid contracts |
| Asia Pacific | 45% | 100% | RECs, on-site |

**Investment:** $85M over 3 years
**Savings:** $15M annually (post-2028)

### Initiative 2: Fleet Electrification

**Scope:** 850 company vehicles

| Phase | Vehicles | Timeline | Investment |
|-------|----------|----------|------------|
| Phase 1 | 250 EVs | 2026 | $8M |
| Phase 2 | 350 EVs | 2027 | $11M |
| Phase 3 | 250 EVs | 2028 | $8M |
| Charging Infrastructure | All sites | 2026-2028 | $5M |

### Initiative 3: Manufacturing Efficiency

**Target:** 30% energy intensity reduction

| Initiative | Investment | Savings | CO2 Reduction |
|------------|------------|---------|---------------|
| HVAC Optimization | $12M | $8M/year | 15,000 tonnes |
| Process Heat Recovery | $18M | $12M/year | 22,000 tonnes |
| LED Lighting | $5M | $3M/year | 8,000 tonnes |
| Building Automation | $8M | $5M/year | 12,000 tonnes |

### Initiative 4: Zero Waste Operations (2028)

**Current:** 28% to landfill | **Target:** 0%

| Stream | Current | 2028 Target | Approach |
|--------|---------|-------------|----------|
| Metal Scrap | 95% recycled | 99% | Enhanced separation |
| Plastic | 45% recycled | 85% | Advanced recycling |
| Paper/Cardboard | 85% recycled | 95% | Process improvement |
| Hazardous | 15% treated | 100% | Treatment investment |
| Composting | 20% | 80% | On-site facilities |

### Initiative 5: Water Stewardship

**Target:** 25% reduction in water intensity

| Initiative | Investment | Savings |
|------------|------------|---------|
| Closed-Loop Cooling | $15M | 500 ML/year |
| Water Recycling | $12M | 350 ML/year |
| Rainwater Harvesting | $5M | 150 ML/year |
| Process Optimization | $8M | 200 ML/year |

